### Suggested defaults (if the repo is new)

If the user hasn’t specified preferences yet, start with these sane defaults:

- Keep code changes small and readable.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Avoid cleverness; optimize for maintainability.
- Add tests for non-trivial logic.

## Testing guidelines

- Keep tests deterministic (avoid timing/network flakiness).
- Prefer unit tests for core logic; add integration tests when needed.
- When fixing a bug, add a regression test.

## Security & privacy

- Do not add secrets to the repository.
- Prefer environment variables or secret managers for credentials.
- Validate and sanitize external input.
- Avoid risky dependencies; pin versions when appropriate.

